  "id": "rate-coding",
  "term": "rate coding",
  "definition": "Rate coding is a way neural activity can represent information mainly through how often spikes occur, rather than through precise rhythmic timing. In the source packet, irregular and semiregular spike patterns are described as contributing primarily to this kind of coding.",
